---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---
<Base title="AI and automation disclosure" description={`How ${SITE.name} uses AI and automation, and where humans decide.`}>
  <div class="plain">
    <div class="page-head"><h1>AI and automation disclosure</h1><p>What is automated here, what is not, and who is responsible.</p></div>
    <h2>In short</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>AI systems assist with research, drafting and production.</li>
      <li>Source verification and editorial rules govern every factual claim.</li>
      <li>Automation is used to monitor and organise gaming information.</li>
      <li>A human Editor-in-Chief approves what is published.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What automation does</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Monitoring.</strong> Software checks official channels, gaming press and community forums for GTA VI developments, groups reports about the same event, and records where each one came from.</li>
      <li><strong>Labelling.</strong> Each story gets a verification label limited by its evidence. The limits are fixed in code: an AI model can lower a label but cannot raise it above what the sources support.</li>
      <li><strong>Drafting.</strong> An AI model drafts articles from an evidence file listing each claim, its source and its date. It is not allowed to add facts from its own memory.</li>
      <li><strong>Checking.</strong> Automated checks flag uncited statements, quotes that do not appear in the evidence, duplicates and thin stories.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What humans do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Decide what is worth covering and what is not.</li>
      <li>Review and approve every article before it is published.</li>
      <li>Handle corrections.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Limits you should know about</h2>
    <p>AI systems make mistakes, including confident ones. That is why each claim is linked to a source you can open yourself, and why uncertain material is labelled as a rumour, theory or community discovery. If you find an error, treat the linked source as the authority, not our summary of it.</p>
    <h2>Byline</h2>
    <p>Articles are credited to "{SITE.byline}", a team byline. We do not present AI-assisted work as the work of a named journalist, and we do not invent people.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
